# Makefile — the scripted path for this project.
#
# YOURS. `agentic-sdlc init` wrote it once and never overwrites it, not even
# with --force. One line is the whole standard set: the include that defines
# every target (`make help` lists them). The kit it runs is the version
# uv.lock pins, installed in .venv.
#
# BUMPING THE PIN is `uv add --dev agentic-sdlc==X.Y.Z`, or a dependency bot's
# PR. Read the release notes, run `make pm ARGS=vocabulary` for what the closed
# state/rule sets became, and `make sdlc ARGS='install-* --diff'` for what the
# shipped files would change before you let them; then
# `make sdlc ARGS='adopt X.Y.Z'`.
include Makefile.devkit

# Your own targets go below, and they are listed by `make help` beside the
# standard ones as long as each carries a `## description` comment:
#
#     my-scan: ## a gate this project owns
#     	@bash tools/dev/checks/my_scan.sh
#
# A gate of your own joins `make check` through devkit.toml — never a fork of
# Makefile.devkit:
#
#     [gates]
#     extra = ["my-scan"]
